            <div xml:id="d598">

                <pb facs="0861" n="745" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg745"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/5108: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-07-27T13:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 27, 1923—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 27—10:03
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>264. Following telegram received from commander of Yangtze patrol dated July
                    23rd.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“On July 17th General Chow, commanding Kweichow troops and guarding the right
                        bank of river opposite Chungking, treacherously revolted and went over to
                        the first army, crossed river and took Kiangpei cutting off Chungking from
                        down river. On July 20th S.S. <hi rendition="#italic">Alice Dollar</hi> was
                        shot at by his troops on her way to Chungking. <pb facs="0862" n="746"
                            xml:id="pg746"/> On July 21st <hi rendition="#italic">Alice Dollar</hi>
                        on departure was escorted by <hi rendition="#italic">Monocacy</hi>,
                        Lieutenant Commander Nielson, both <hi rendition="#italic">Alice Dollar</hi>
                        and <hi rendition="#italic">Monocacy</hi> were shot at. <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Monocacy</hi> returned the [fire] with her battery.
                        Attack on American flag wholly unjustified and unprovoked. On July 22nd <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Palos</hi> reported conditions normal at Chungking;
                        General Chow Hsi-cheng has retreated to Kweichow. It would appear that <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Monocacy</hi> action has defeated a forcible attempt
                        to establish an illegal blockade of the river whereby foreign community in
                        Chungking would have been cut off.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                    >Bell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
